<Size><T>Double</T><D>125</D></Size></Item>
<Item XName="Page" Type="PageMgr">
<Item XName="Display0" Type="FunctionDisp">
<DVport><T>Array_Dbl64</T><D>1;4;;;qu14;ub14</D></DVport>
<PVPort><T>Array_Dbl64</T><D>1;4;;;E7vRapoXr24;M1O5Wh{Y24</D></PVPort>
<Show><T>Bool</T><D>0</D></Show>
<ShowCmd><T>Int</T><D>1</D></ShowCmd>
<Split><T>Double</T><D>0.3</D></Split>
<Window><T>Array_I64</T><D>1;4;;t3;i6;m7</D></Window>
<ZOrder><T>Int</T><D>9</D></ZOrder></Item></Item></Item>
<Item XName="lla2ecf" UserName="lla2ecf" Type="function">
<Selected><T>Bool</T><D>0</D></Selected>
<Text>%% lla to xyz&#x000D;&#x000A;% input parameter : [longitude, latitude, height]&#x000D;&#x000A;% output parameter : ecf frame [x, y, z];&#x000D;&#x000A;&#x000D;&#x000A;function ecf = lla2ecf(lla_coordinate)&#x000D;&#x000A;Ra = 6378137;   % unit : m&#x000D;&#x000A;Rb = 6356752;   % unit : m&#x000D;&#x000A;f = (Ra - Rb) / Ra;&#x000D;&#x000A;e2 = 2 * f - f * f;&#x000D;&#x000A;e = sqrt(e2);&#x000D;&#x000A;we = 7.29211515e-5; % unit: rad/second&#x000D;&#x000A;&#x000D;&#x000A;lambda = lla_coordinate(1);&#x000D;&#x000A;phi = lla_coordinate(2);&#x000D;&#x000A;h = lla_coordinate(3);&#x000D;&#x000A;&#x000D;&#x000A;N = Ra / sqrt(1 - e2 * sin(phi*pi/180));&#x000D;&#x000A;&#x000D;&#x000A;x = (N + h) * cos(phi*pi/180) * cos(lambda*pi/180);&#x000D;&#x000A;y = (N + h) * cos(phi*pi/180) * sin(lambda*pi/180);&#x000D;&#x000A;z = (N * (1 - e2) + h) * sin(phi*pi/180);&#x000D;&#x000A;&#x000D;&#x000A;ecf = zeros(1,3);&#x000D;&#x000A;ecf(1) = x;&#x000D;&#x000A;ecf(2) = y;&#x000D;&#x000A;ecf(3) = z;&#x000D;&#x000A;&#x000D;&#x000A;end&#x000D;&#x000A;</Text>
<Item XName="BPMgr" Type="BPMgr">
<BPLines><T>Empty</T></BPLines>
<BPStates><T>Empty</T></BPStates></Item>
<Item XName="Font" Type="Font">
<Name>Courier New</Name>
<Size><T>Double</T><D>125</D></Size></Item>
<Item XName="Page" Type="PageMgr">
<Item XName="Display0" Type="FunctionDisp">
<DVport><T>Array_Dbl64</T><D>1;4;;;qu14;ub14</D></DVport>
<PVPort><T>Array_Dbl64</T><D>1;4;;;E7vRapoXr24;M1O5Wh{Y24</D></PVPort>
<Show><T>Bool</T><D>0</D></Show>
<ShowCmd><T>Int</T><D>1</D></ShowCmd>
<Split><T>Double</T><D>0.3</D></Split>
<Window><T>Array_I64</T><D>1;4;;m7;i6;fB</D></Window>
<ZOrder><T>Int</T><D>8</D></ZOrder></Item></Item></Item></Item>
<Item XName="Page" Type="PageMgr" />
<Item XName="Read Me to understand this example" UserName="Read Me to understand this example" Type="Notes">
<Selected><T>Bool</T><D>0</D></Selected>
<Text>&lt;FONT size=2&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 18pt; FONT-FAMILY: Arial&quot;&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoTitle style=&quot;BORDER-TOP: medium none; BORDER-RIGHT: medium none; BORDER-BOTTOM: windowtext 0.75pt solid; PADDING-BOTTOM: 1pt; PADDING-TOP: 0in; PADDING-LEFT: 0in; BORDER-LEFT: medium none; MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt; PADDING-RIGHT: 0in&quot; align=center&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;FONT size=2&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT size=4&gt;&lt;FONT face=Calibri&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;&lt;FONT size=6&gt;Simulation Template for Phased Array Doppler Radar &lt;BR&gt;with EW Jammer&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 10pt&quot; align=center&gt;&lt;FONT size=4&gt;Keysight Technologies SystemVue Example Workspace&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 10pt&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT size=5&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 10pt&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT color=#ff0000 size=5&gt;This workspace has been saved without simulation data to reduce its size. Please run the simulation to see the data in the graphs.&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 10pt&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT size=5&gt;This example uses simulation models&amp;nbsp;from the W1905 Radar library, and also the W1720 Phased Array Beamforming Kit, which is included with the Radar library.&amp;nbsp; There are several things for you to explore:&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;OL&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;LI&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;DIV class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 10pt&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT size=5 face=Arial&gt;Vary the Pulsed Doppler Radar architecture in terms of its signaling parameters&lt;BR&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; Pulse Width, PRF, Carrier frequency, Sample Rate, Pulse compression ratio&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/DIV&gt;&lt;/LI&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;LI&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;DIV class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 10pt&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT size=5 face=Arial&gt;Explore the phased array architecture:&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;BR&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; Number of Elements, Geometry of the elements, spacing between the elements&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/DIV&gt;&lt;/LI&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;LI&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;DIV class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 10pt&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT size=5 face=Arial&gt;Study the effect of the EW jammer, noise and clutter (in future).&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/DIV&gt;&lt;/LI&gt;&lt;/OL&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 10pt&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT size=5&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 10pt&quot;&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;&lt;FONT size=5&gt;Simple tests to do out of box.&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;OL&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;LI&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;DIV class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 10pt&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT size=5 face=Arial&gt;Run the script &quot;Scenario_Simulation&quot; from the workspace (right-click on the workspace icon, then &quot;Run Equations&quot;).&amp;nbsp; Observe the plots of Tx beam, Rx beam, Jammer beam and Doppler plot. Note the agreement of the computed and set ranges.&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/DIV&gt;&lt;/LI&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;LI&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;DIV class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 10pt&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT size=5 face=Arial&gt;Vary the parameters in the tune window (make sure you hit enter after changing the values) and run the above script again.&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/DIV&gt;&lt;/LI&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;LI&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;DIV class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 10pt&quot;&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;FONT size=5 face=Arial&gt;Find the angles and power of jammer at which the radar can be immune or susceptible.&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/DIV&gt;&lt;/LI&gt;&lt;/OL&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;</Text>
<Item XName="Page" Type="PageMgr">
<Item XName="Display0" Type="NotesDisp">
<DVport><T>Array_Dbl64</T><D>1;4;;;e324;Wu14</D></DVport>
<PVPort><T>Array_Dbl64</T><D>1;4;;;Ja8HY4r6w24;8GW012yIm24</D></PVPort>
<Show><T>Bool</T><D>1</D></Show>
<ShowCmd><T>Int</T><D>1</D></ShowCmd>
<Window><T>Array_I64</T><D>1;4;;;8A;p6</D></Window>
<ZOrder><T>Int</T><D>0</D></ZOrder></Item></Item></Item>
